  "final": "Done. The cause was in `billing/totals.py`. `line_total_cents` used float math and Python's `round()`. Floats can't represent values like 1.005 or 2.675 exactly, and `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even number, so some rows came out one cent low. The README says amounts round half up.\n\nI switched the calculation to `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Spot checks now give 1.005 → 101 cents and 2.675 → 268 cents. `python3 -m unittest` ran 6 tests and all passed. I didn't add a regression test for the half-cent cases.",
